# VATS Boss API

The handbook lives only in `docs/vendor/itoolabs/` on the developer machine. That directory is gitignored and dockerignored. Do not commit it or long quotations. The GitHub repository is public.

Object paths in code are literals from that handbook. Do not accept an operation, path, or body field from a caller, a flag, or the saved catalog. Do not invent methods. This is REST, not SOAP, and it is not the RTU API.

This release may send only:

- `GET /sys/boss/v1/domains`
- `GET /sys/boss/v1/domains/{domain}`
- `GET /sys/boss/v1/domains/{domain}/stat`
- `PUT /sys/boss/v1/domains/{domain}` whose JSON body is exactly `{client}` or `{language}`
- `GET /sys/boss/v1/telnums`
- `GET /sys/boss/v1/telnums/{telnum}`
- `GET /sys/boss/v1/gateways`
- `GET /sys/boss/v1/routes`
- `GET /sys/boss/v1/dialplans`

The statistics read is one GET after that domain's card. The lock is released between the two requests. Store only `recordExpirationDays` and `speechAnalytics.thisMonth`, each a non-negative safe integer. A 403, a 404, or a body that is not an object keeps the previous two numbers, and the domain is still published. That miss is not one of the five unread cards. A 401 stops the cycle. A transport failure, timeout, empty body, non-JSON, or 5xx does not publish the domain section. Do not call `GET /domains/{domain}/services`. Do not store `activeCRM`, `telnumsCount`, services, accessURL, or route.

Language values sent by the client are only `ru-RU` or `en-US`. The domain is path-encoded. Reject `/` and `..`. Do not echo dialplan, route, services, limits, billing, name, or any other field. If the platform rejects the one-field body, show the error and do not send a second request. After a 204, read the same card. Success only if that one field changed and the rest matches the pre-image. Do not send a compensating `PUT`.

The domain write is sent only by the button «Изменить» after a dialog that shows the domain, the field, the old value, and the new value. Settings are saved only by the confirm button, which shows the host and the login and not the password. Cancel, close, and Enter do not send. «Проверить доступ» is one `GET /domains` and needs no confirm dialog. It does not write the snapshot and does not start the card walk.

One in-process timer reads the platform. The first pass is 5 seconds after the scheduler starts, then 120 seconds after the previous pass finishes. The pass is not a job-queue action. One Boss request is in flight at a time, through one FIFO lock shared by the walk and by operator card reads. A transport failure, or more than five unread cards, does not publish that section. Up to five missing cards keep the previous fields and the section still publishes. An empty or truncated list does not wipe a non-empty snapshot. A list from another host is hidden and must not be used in `PUT`.

Do not call POST, DELETE, HEAD, freeze, unfreeze, allocate, deallocate, assign, enable, disable, block, services, call directions, caller-id forwarding, gateway, dialplan, or route changes, create domain, create number, `GET /generatepassword`, `GET .../session`, `GET .../isfrozen`, or `GET /users/{login}/auth`. «Сотрудники» stays out of the nav until that page exists. A later employee edit may change only realName, position, and email, with the same confirm and readback. Do not add any other Boss operation.

HTTPS origin only, no path and no userinfo. Do not follow redirects. Do not trust a custom certificate. GET may retry once. PUT never retries. Body cap 20 MB. Timeout 30s.

The password is ciphertext at rest and is sent only as `Authorization: Basic` to the pinned host. Do not log the password, the header, a session link, or the SOAP-style envelope. API keys cannot call these routes. Do not change RTU, CDR, or SMG behavior.
